{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "10", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "23", "M": "31", "S": "00"}}, "news": [{"title": "Twenty three years on, Bengaluru\u2019s 1,134 Arkavathy Layout allottees still await sites", "para": "Over a thousand original Arkavathy Layout allottees remain without sites after twenty-three years. The Bangalore Development Authority originally planned twenty thousand sites for this project. Litigation and denotification scandals significantly reduced the available plots for allotment. Many affected individuals have pursued legal recourse and presented evidence. The BDA continues efforts to accommodate remaining allottees as litigation resolves.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/twenty-three-years-on-bengalurus-1134-arkavathy-layout-allottees-still-await-sites/134000053?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-103/134000053.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Identify land parcels for student PGs: LG to Delhi development body", "para": "The Delhi government is set to launch a new initiative aimed at ensuring safe and budget-friendly paying guest accommodations for students. Under the directive of the Lieutenant Governor, the DDA is tasked with locating appropriate land for this purpose. Collaborations between universities and external providers are planned for optimized student housing.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/identify-land-parcels-for-student-pgs-lg-to-delhi-development-body/133999793?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-277240/133999793.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Green NOCs missing, Uttar Pradesh pollution control board shut 15 hotels, restaurants in last two years", "para": "In a decisive action against pollution in the region, the UP Pollution Control Board has mandated the closure of fifteen hotels and restaurants. Additionally, show-cause notices have been issued to fifty-eight more establishments following a thorough review. Out of 625 establishments in Ghaziabad, only 241 have been surveyed so far. For those that didn\u2019t comply, closure orders have been enforced, and electricity connections cut.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/hospitality/green-nocs-missing-uttar-pradesh-pollution-control-board-shut-15-hotels-restaurants-in-last-two-years/133999868?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-199350/133999868.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "hospitality"}]}